        {
            "id": "node_f0e65f16-ef59-4faf-8041-13e0af3a7525",
            "name": "indexDeclarations",
            "kind": "Processor",
            "parentId": "node_904ae018-f319-47f2-9e50-420176470c23",
            "children": [],
            "incomingLinks": [
                "link_311e146e-a6d2-40dd-a5a7-ea39a79db747",
                "link_31ef8acc-8bab-4b8a-bf30-b326032e09f9",
                "link_8e9116b6-3525-4cd6-8226-8dd9ebcf3c2b"
            ],
            "outgoingLinks": [
                "link_755deaa9-863e-410f-b2c2-06e9c6d0732b",
                "link_e32de3c2-877f-4805-9202-aa5c51b3ec69",
                "link_63cd6ec2-47fc-4c44-87b9-b3e6554046bb",
                "link_371c96cc-fc27-4ee2-ba8d-7d0aff0f8eb6"
            ],
            "layout": {
                "x": 3348.0,
                "y": -1246.0,
                "width": 240.0,
                "height": 168.0,
                "closedWidth": 240.0,
                "closedHeight": 168.0,
                "openWidth": 240.0,
                "openHeight": 168.0,
                "isExpanded": true
            },
            "fileLayoutStrategyId": "none",
            "text": {
                "initialization": "",
                "initializationLanguageId": "",
                "source": "fun indexDeclarations(cplusAst, cplusAst2, moduleResolutionService3) {\n  val packet1 = pop(\"cplusAst\")\n  val packet2 = pop(\"cplusAst2\")\n  val outcome = moduleResolutionService3.invokeIndexDeclarations(packet1, packet2)\n  when (outcome) {\n    is Success -> {\n    push(\"catalogue3\", outcome.value)\n    push(\"catalogue4\", outcome.value)\n    push(\"catalogue2\", outcome.value)\n    push(\"catalogue\", outcome.value)\n    }\n    is Failure -> {\n    return outcome\n    }\n  }\n}",
                "sourceLanguageId": "kotlin",
                "specification": "# indexDeclarations\n\n## Functional role\n\nThis entity is a callable processing function in the runFrontEnd composite. Its name is a verb because it performs the operation; it is not a prototype and does not own the bulk algorithm.\n\n## Technical contract\n\n- Function signature: `indexDeclarations(cplusAst, cplusAst2, moduleResolutionService3)`.\n- Incoming links are noun-named channels materialized as function arguments: `cplusAst`, `cplusAst2`, `moduleResolutionService3`.\n- Data arguments hold packet or object-prototype instances. The function MUST pop each data channel before invoking the library.\n- Library argument: `moduleResolutionService3`, supplied by the `lib_module_resolution` library suite.\n- The function invokes one coherent library operation `invokeIndexDeclarations(...)` and routes its Operation<T,E> result.\n- Success packets are pushed to outgoing noun-named channels: `catalogue3`, `catalogue4`, `catalogue2`, `catalogue`.\n- Expected failures are routed to the returned failure; failures MUST NOT be hidden.\n- Parsing, resolution, evaluation, lowering, emission, and workspace algorithms belong in the library suite, not in this node.",
                "specificationLanguageId": "markdown",
                "tests": "{\"cases\":[]}",
                "testsLanguageId": "json",
                "aiInstructions": "",
                "aiInstructionsLanguageId": "markdown"
            },
            "binaryContent": null,
            "technology": {
                "languageId": "",
                "technologyId": "",
