                "sourceLanguageId": "kotlin",
                "specification": "# library_moduleResolution\n\n## Functional role\n\nThis library contains a free-standing function suite for module Resolution. It boxes reusable functions and algorithms used by processing functions.\n\n## Identifier convention\n\nThe library identifier MUST be prefixed with `lib_` or `library_`, or suffixed with `_lib` or `_library`. This library uses the required `library_` prefix: `library_moduleResolution`.\n\n## Technical contract\n\n- Exposes a `service` capability containing the free-standing function suite.\n- Its functions are free-standing and may encapsulate suite state and external I/O.\n- Owns the bulk algorithm, reusable policy, adapters, and coherent failure behavior for its suite.\n- Processing nodes receive this capability through a library argument link and invoke one operation per packet batch; they MUST NOT duplicate these algorithms.\n- Results use `Operation<T,E>` so expected errors can be routed as diagnostic packets.",
                "specificationLanguageId": "markdown",
                "tests": "{\"cases\":[]}",
