            "fileLayoutStrategyId": "none",
            "text": {
                "initialization": "",
                "initializationLanguageId": "",
                "source": "fun resolveSymbolsAndScopes(resolvedImports, semanticResolutionService, scopes, catalogue4) {\n  val packet1 = pop(\"resolvedImports\")\n  val packet2 = pop(\"scopes\")\n  val packet3 = pop(\"catalogue4\")\n  val outcome = semanticResolutionService.invokeResolveSymbolsAndScopes(packet1, packet2, packet3)\n  when (outcome) {\n    is Success -> {\n    push(\"semanticModel4\", outcome.value)\n    push(\"semanticModel\", outcome.value)\n    push(\"semanticModel3\", outcome.value)\n    push(\"semanticModel2\", outcome.value)\n    }\n    is Failure -> {\n    return outcome\n    }\n  }\n}",
                "sourceLanguageId": "kotlin",
                "specification": "# resolveSymbolsAndScopes\n\n## Functional role\n\nThis entity is a callable processing function in the resolveSemanticModel composite. Its name is a verb because it performs the operation; it is not a prototype and does not own the bulk algorithm.\n\n## Technical contract\n\n- Function signature: `resolveSymbolsAndScopes(resolvedImports, semanticResolutionService, scopes, catalogue4)`.\n- Incoming links are noun-named channels materialized as function arguments: `resolvedImports`, `semanticResolutionService`, `scopes`, `catalogue4`.\n- Data arguments hold packet or object-prototype instances. The function MUST pop each data channel before invoking the library.\n- Library argument: `semanticResolutionService`, supplied by the `library_semanticResolution` library suite.\n- The function invokes one coherent library operation `invokeResolveSymbolsAndScopes(...)` and routes its Operation<T,E> result.\n- Success packets are pushed to outgoing noun-named channels: `semanticModel4`, `semanticModel`, `semanticModel3`, `semanticModel2`.\n- Expected failures are routed to the returned failure; failures MUST NOT be hidden.\n- Parsing, resolution, evaluation, lowering, emission, and workspace algorithms belong in the library suite, not in this node.",
                "specificationLanguageId": "markdown",
                "tests": "{\"cases\":[]}",
                "testsLanguageId": "json",
