        {
            "id": "node_b321a52d-6f83-4d97-84b9-5b9ef4cc9905",
            "name": "indexReferences",
            "kind": "Processor",
            "parentId": "node_c812b9ff-7520-478b-a1ab-4f1a311b9411",
            "children": [],
            "incomingLinks": [
                "link_6fd3be9d-22d5-471e-bf83-7c5f2f5240df",
                "link_727410cd-787b-4806-b9b7-88caea907201"
            ],
            "outgoingLinks": [
                "link_69e0151a-db39-40aa-9f7b-6c23d246b308"
            ],
            "layout": {
                "x": 11649.0,
                "y": -1710.0,
                "width": 240.0,
                "height": 78.0,
                "closedWidth": 240.0,
                "closedHeight": 78.0,
                "openWidth": 240.0,
                "openHeight": 78.0,
                "isExpanded": true
            },
            "fileLayoutStrategyId": "none",
            "text": {
                "initialization": "",
                "initializationLanguageId": "",
                "source": "fun indexReferences(semanticModel, sourceFileService3) {\n  val packet1 = pop(\"semanticModel\")\n  val outcome = sourceFileService3.invokeIndexReferences(packet1)\n  when (outcome) {\n    is Success -> {\n    push(\"references\", outcome.value)\n    }\n    is Failure -> {\n    return outcome\n    }\n  }\n}",
                "sourceLanguageId": "kotlin",
                "specification": "# indexReferences\n\n## Functional role\n\nThis entity is a callable processing function in the resolveSemanticModel composite. Its name is a verb because it performs the operation; it is not a prototype and does not own the bulk algorithm.\n\n## Technical contract\n\n- Function signature: `indexReferences(semanticModel, sourceFileService3)`.\n- Incoming links are noun-named channels materialized as function arguments: `semanticModel`, `sourceFileService3`.\n- Data arguments hold packet or object-prototype instances. The function MUST pop each data channel before invoking the library.\n- Library argument: `sourceFileService3`, supplied by the `lib_source_files` library suite.\n- The function invokes one coherent library operation `invokeIndexReferences(...)` and routes its Operation<T,E> result.\n- Success packets are pushed to outgoing noun-named channels: `references`.\n- Expected failures are routed to the returned failure; failures MUST NOT be hidden.\n- Parsing, resolution, evaluation, lowering, emission, and workspace algorithms belong in the library suite, not in this node.",
                "specificationLanguageId": "markdown",
                "tests": "{\"cases\":[]}",
                "testsLanguageId": "json",
