                "source": "fun createCompilerContext(toolingService, workspace) {\n  val packet1 = pop(\"workspace\")\n  val outcome = toolingService.invokeCreateCompilerContext(packet1)\n  when (outcome) {\n    is Success -> {\n    return outcome\n    }\n    is Failure -> {\n    return outcome\n    }\n  }\n}",
                "sourceLanguageId": "kotlin",
                "specification": "# createCompilerContext\n\n## Functional role\n\nThis entity is a callable processing function in the serveCompilerTooling composite. Its name is a verb because it performs the operation; it is not a prototype and does not own the bulk algorithm.\n\n## Technical contract\n\n- Function signature: `createCompilerContext(toolingService, workspace)`.\n- Incoming links are noun-named channels materialized as function arguments: `toolingService`, `workspace`.\n- Data arguments hold packet or object-prototype instances. The function MUST pop each data channel before invoking the library.\n- Library argument: `toolingService`, supplied by the `library_toolingServices` library suite.\n- The function invokes one coherent library operation `invokeCreateCompilerContext(...)` and routes its Operation<T,E> result.\n- Success packets are pushed to outgoing noun-named channels: none.\n- Expected failures are routed to the returned failure; failures MUST NOT be hidden.\n- Parsing, resolution, evaluation, lowering, emission, and workspace algorithms belong in the library suite, not in this node.",
