        {
            "id": "node_37a2c377-bed6-4d88-b84b-4059e4aaa168",
            "name": "CSubsetAst",
            "kind": "Type",
            "parentId": "root",
            "children": [],
            "incomingLinks": [],
            "outgoingLinks": [],
            "layout": {
                "x": 17010.0,
                "y": 305.0,
                "width": 294.0,
                "height": 300.0,
                "closedWidth": 294.0,
                "closedHeight": 300.0,
                "openWidth": 294.0,
                "openHeight": 300.0,
                "isExpanded": true
            },
            "fileLayoutStrategyId": "none",
            "text": {
                "initialization": "",
                "initializationLanguageId": "",
                "source": "",
                "sourceLanguageId": "kotlin",
                "specification": "# CSubsetAst\n\n## Functional role\n\n`CSubsetAst` is an object-instance prototype for structured compiler packets. Instances cross function boundaries through noun-named channels; the prototype contains data and invariants, not behavior.\n\n## Field contract\n\n| Field | Type | Storage | Meaning |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| dialect | String | value | Selected C dialect and feature profile. |\n| includes | List<CInclude> | value | Normalized system and project include directives. |\n| declarations | List<CDeclaration> | value | C declarations in deterministic source order. |\n| definitions | List<CDefinition> | value | C definitions and lowered function bodies. |\n| dependencies | List<CDependency> | value | Referenced declarations and emission dependencies. |\n| sourceOrigins | SourceAndOriginModel | prototype reference | Origin information retained through lowering. |\n| symbolNames | Map<SymbolId,String> | value | Deterministic generated C names. |\n| diagnostics | List<Diagnostic> | prototype reference | Backend diagnostics attached to the C representation. |\n\n## Technical contract\n\n- The qualifier is `object`; each packet is an independently owned instance.\n- Fields with stable identifiers MUST preserve identity across incremental compilation.\n- Source ranges and origin fields MUST remain usable for diagnostics, navigation, and generated-code mapping.\n- Processing nodes may pop and push instances of this prototype, while libraries create, transform, validate, and persist them.\n- Type identifiers use PascalCase; algorithms remain in libraries.",
                "specificationLanguageId": "markdown",
                "tests": "{\"cases\":[]}",
                "testsLanguageId": "json",
                "aiInstructions": "",
                "aiInstructionsLanguageId": "markdown"
            },
            "binaryContent": null,
            "technology": {
