                "specification": "# Diagnostic\n\n## Functional role\n\n`Diagnostic` is an object-instance prototype for structured compiler packets. Instances cross function boundaries through noun-named channels; the prototype contains data and invariants, not behavior.\n\n## Field contract\n\n| Field | Type | Storage | Meaning |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| severity | DiagnosticSeverity | value | Error, warning, information, or hint classification. |\n| code | String | value | Stable machine-readable diagnostic code. |\n| message | String | value | Human-readable diagnostic message. |\n| phase | String | value | Compiler phase that produced the diagnostic. |\n| sourceFile | String | value | Source URI when the diagnostic has a source location. |\n| range | SourceRange | value | Primary source range, if mapped. |\n| origin | SourceOrigin | value | Origin record for generated or transformed code. |\n| relatedDiagnostics | List<Diagnostic> | prototype reference | Related notes and secondary locations. |\n| fixes | List<CodeFix> | prototype reference | Optional machine-applicable repairs. |\n\n## Technical contract\n\n- The qualifier is `object`; each packet is an independently owned instance.\n- Fields with stable identifiers MUST preserve identity across incremental compilation.\n- Source ranges and origin fields MUST remain usable for diagnostics, navigation, and generated-code mapping.\n- Processing nodes may pop and push instances of this prototype, while libraries create, transform, validate, and persist them.\n- Type identifiers use PascalCase; algorithms remain in libraries.",
                "specificationLanguageId": "markdown",
                "tests": "{\"cases\":[]}",
                "testsLanguageId": "json",
                "aiInstructions": "",
                "aiInstructionsLanguageId": "markdown"
            },
