            "fileLayoutStrategyId": "none",
            "text": {
                "initialization": "",
                "initializationLanguageId": "",
                "source": "",
                "sourceLanguageId": "kotlin",
                "specification": "# SourceAndOriginModel\n\n## Functional role\n\n`SourceAndOriginModel` is an object-instance prototype for structured compiler packets. Instances cross function boundaries through noun-named channels; the prototype contains data and invariants, not behavior.\n\n## Field contract\n\n| Field | Type | Storage | Meaning |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| workspaceRoot | String | value | Canonical workspace root used to resolve source URIs. |\n| sourceFiles | List<SourceFile> | value | Ordered source files with stable URI and content identity. |\n| lineIndexes | Map<SourceFileId,LineIndex> | value | Line and column indexes for every source file. |\n| origins | Map<NodeId,SourceOrigin> | value | Stable origin records attached to syntax and generated nodes. |\n| revision | String | value | Monotonic source snapshot revision. |\n\n## Technical contract\n\n- The qualifier is `object`; each packet is an independently owned instance.\n- Fields with stable identifiers MUST preserve identity across incremental compilation.\n- Source ranges and origin fields MUST remain usable for diagnostics, navigation, and generated-code mapping.\n- Processing nodes may pop and push instances of this prototype, while libraries create, transform, validate, and persist them.\n- Type identifiers use PascalCase; algorithms remain in libraries.",
                "specificationLanguageId": "markdown",
                "tests": "{\"cases\":[]}",
                "testsLanguageId": "json",
                "aiInstructions": "",
                "aiInstructionsLanguageId": "markdown"
            },
            "binaryContent": null,
