            "text": {
                "initialization": "",
                "initializationLanguageId": "",
                "source": "",
                "sourceLanguageId": "kotlin",
                "specification": "# SourceMap\n\n## Functional role\n\n`SourceMap` is an object-instance prototype for structured compiler packets. Instances cross function boundaries through noun-named channels; the prototype contains data and invariants, not behavior.\n\n## Field contract\n\n| Field | Type | Storage | Meaning |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| generatedFile | String | value | Generated artifact URI. |\n| sourceFiles | List<String> | value | Source URIs referenced by the artifact. |\n| entries | List<SourceMapEntry> | value | Generated-to-source range mappings. |\n| originIndex | Map<GeneratedRange,SourceRange> | value | Fast lookup from generated ranges to source ranges. |\n| diagnosticAnchors | Map<String,SourceRange> | value | Stable anchors for mapped external diagnostics. |\n| version | String | value | Source-map schema version. |\n\n## Technical contract\n\n- The qualifier is `object`; each packet is an independently owned instance.\n- Fields with stable identifiers MUST preserve identity across incremental compilation.\n- Source ranges and origin fields MUST remain usable for diagnostics, navigation, and generated-code mapping.\n- Processing nodes may pop and push instances of this prototype, while libraries create, transform, validate, and persist them.\n- Type identifiers use PascalCase; algorithms remain in libraries.",
                "specificationLanguageId": "markdown",
                "tests": "{\"cases\":[]}",
                "testsLanguageId": "json",
                "aiInstructions": "",
