            "fileLayoutStrategyId": "none",
            "text": {
                "initialization": "",
                "initializationLanguageId": "",
                "source": "",
                "sourceLanguageId": "kotlin",
                "specification": "# LineIndex\n\n## Functional role\n\n`LineIndex` is an object-instance prototype used by compiler functions and libraries. A compact line and column index for a source file.\n\n## Field contract\n\n| Field | Type | Storage | Meaning |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| lineStarts | List<Int> | value | Zero-based offsets for line starts. |\n| encoding | String | value | Character encoding used for columns. |\n| lineCount | Int | value | Number of indexed lines. |\n\n## Technical contract\n\n- The qualifier is `object`; instances are values transported through noun-named channels.\n- Stable identifiers and source ranges MUST remain deterministic across incremental compilation.\n- References to other declared prototypes are explicit in the field type contract.\n- Processing nodes route instances; libraries create, validate, transform, and persist them.\n- The prototype contains data and invariants, not executable behavior.",
                "specificationLanguageId": "markdown",
                "tests": "{\"cases\":[]}",
                "testsLanguageId": "json",
                "aiInstructions": "",
                "aiInstructionsLanguageId": "markdown"
            },
            "binaryContent": null,
