            "text": {
                "initialization": "",
                "initializationLanguageId": "",
                "source": "",
                "sourceLanguageId": "kotlin",
                "specification": "# SourceFile\n\n## Functional role\n\n`SourceFile` is an object-instance prototype used by compiler functions and libraries. A source artifact and its stable content identity.\n\n## Field contract\n\n| Field | Type | Storage | Meaning |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| id | SourceFileId | prototype reference | Stable object identifier. |\n| uri | String | value | Canonical source URI. |\n| text | String | value | Source contents for the snapshot. |\n| contentHash | String | value | Content identity hash. |\n| languageId | String | value | Language or dialect identifier. |\n| version | String | value | Source snapshot version. |\n| isGenerated | Boolean | value | Whether the artifact was generated. |\n\n## Technical contract\n\n- The qualifier is `object`; instances are values transported through noun-named channels.\n- Stable identifiers and source ranges MUST remain deterministic across incremental compilation.\n- References to other declared prototypes are explicit in the field type contract.\n- Processing nodes route instances; libraries create, validate, transform, and persist them.\n- The prototype contains data and invariants, not executable behavior.",
                "specificationLanguageId": "markdown",
                "tests": "{\"cases\":[]}",
                "testsLanguageId": "json",
                "aiInstructions": "",
                "aiInstructionsLanguageId": "markdown"
