                "isExpanded": true
            },
            "fileLayoutStrategyId": "none",
            "text": {
                "initialization": "",
                "initializationLanguageId": "",
                "source": "",
                "sourceLanguageId": "kotlin",
                "specification": "# CDefinition\n\n## Functional role\n\n`CDefinition` is an object-instance prototype used by compiler functions and libraries. A definition and lowered body in the C-subset representation.\n\n## Field contract\n\n| Field | Type | Storage | Meaning |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| name | String | value | Human-readable symbol or item name. |\n| declarationName | String | value | Declaration associated with the definition. |\n| bodyText | String | value | Lowered C body text. |\n| origin | SourceOrigin | prototype reference | Structured value used by the compiler contract. |\n| dependencies | List<CDependency> | value | Referenced C dependencies. |\n\n## Technical contract\n\n- The qualifier is `object`; instances are values transported through noun-named channels.\n- Stable identifiers and source ranges MUST remain deterministic across incremental compilation.\n- References to other declared prototypes are explicit in the field type contract.\n- Processing nodes route instances; libraries create, validate, transform, and persist them.\n- The prototype contains data and invariants, not executable behavior.",
                "specificationLanguageId": "markdown",
                "tests": "{\"cases\":[]}",
                "testsLanguageId": "json",
                "aiInstructions": "",
                "aiInstructionsLanguageId": "markdown"
            },
            "binaryContent": null,
