                "source": "",
                "sourceLanguageId": "kotlin",
                "specification": "# SourceMapEntry\n\n## Functional role\n\n`SourceMapEntry` is an object-instance prototype used by compiler functions and libraries. A single generated-to-source mapping entry.\n\n## Field contract\n\n| Field | Type | Storage | Meaning |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| generatedRange | GeneratedRange | prototype reference | Generated output range. |\n| sourceRange | SourceRange | prototype reference | Original source range. |\n| sourceOrigin | SourceOrigin | prototype reference | Provenance for the mapped item. |\n| symbolName | String | value | Generated symbol name. |\n\n## Technical contract\n\n- The qualifier is `object`; instances are values transported through noun-named channels.\n- Stable identifiers and source ranges MUST remain deterministic across incremental compilation.\n- References to other declared prototypes are explicit in the field type contract.\n- Processing nodes route instances; libraries create, validate, transform, and persist them.\n- The prototype contains data and invariants, not executable behavior.",
