            "text": {
                "initialization": "",
                "initializationLanguageId": "",
                "source": "",
                "sourceLanguageId": "kotlin",
                "specification": "# Parent\n\n## Functional role\n\n`Parent` is an object-instance prototype that owns an ordered collection of `Child` instances.\n\n## Field contract\n\n| Field | Type | Storage | Meaning |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| id | String | value | Stable parent identifier. |\n| name | String | value | Human-readable parent name. |\n| children | List<Child> | prototype reference | Ordered child instances owned by the parent. |\n\n## Technical contract\n\n- The qualifier is `object`; this declaration describes instances, not executable behavior.\n- `children` is an explicit generic reference to the stable `Child` type declaration.\n- Processing nodes route `Parent` instances through noun-named channels; libraries construct and validate them.\n- The prototype contains data and invariants, not executable behavior.",
                "specificationLanguageId": "markdown",
                "tests": "{\"cases\":[]}",
                "testsLanguageId": "json",
                "aiInstructions": "",
                "aiInstructionsLanguageId": "markdown"
            },
